<article class="env-definition" id="0157">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0157">Definition <span data-tag="0157">13.15.3</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/05T4" data-tag="05T4">13.15.1</a>. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The <em>right derived functors of $F$</em> are the partial functors $RF$ associated to cases (1) and (2) of Situation <a href="/tag/05T4" data-tag="05T4">13.15.1</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The <em>left derived functors of $F$</em> are the partial functors $LF$ associated to cases (3) and (4) of Situation <a href="/tag/05T4" data-tag="05T4">13.15.1</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
An object $A$ of $\mathcal{A}$ is said to be <em>right acyclic for $F$</em>, or <em>acyclic for $RF$</em> if $A[0]$ computes $RF$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
An object $A$ of $\mathcal{A}$ is said to be <em>left acyclic for $F$</em>, or <em>acyclic for $LF$</em> if $A[0]$ computes $LF$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>